{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"9da6ca49e0a2b816bf578ae1890f90a6d30c554cfbfb99a2d5eaa6d91b3b2fd0","digest":{"component_or_area":"CI gate and module-size enforcement","key_entities":[".github/module-size-limit.txt",".github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml",".github/workflows/test.yml","src/rebar/**/*.py","tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py","tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py","refs/remotes/gh-main","github.repository"],"problem_keywords":["module-size gate","enforcement","absolute cap","admin-locked limit","grandfathering escape hatch"],"propositions":["The module-size gate must be rewritten to read an absolute cap from a single limit file instead of using an allowlist-based grandfathering mechanism.","The limit must be locked so it cannot be changed via normal contribution process; only explicit admin override (via git force-push) can modify it.","The gate must fetch main's tip by explicit GitHub URL to detect limit changes and fail with an override error if the limit differs from main's version.","The gate must fail if the limit file is missing, reads NEITHER the allowlist NOR the ceilings file, and warns (not silently) on fetch failure.","The contract and parity tests must be updated to validate the new limit-file mechanism and confirm both workflows read the same single source of truth."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787590262574246001,"uuid":"4a96e369-44f5-4a12-b880-d2ce0dfb9b85"}